EFG 2 R "Chainstore paradox (McKelvey and Palfrey 1998, Figure 1b), 'strategic' version" { "Entrant" "Incumbent" }
"The 'strategic' version of the one-shot chainstore paradox stage game, as
presented in :cite:p:`McKPal98`, Figure 1(b): the incumbent (player 2) must
commit to Fight or Acquiesce without observing the entrant's move, represented
here as a single information set spanning both of the entrant's actions. This
game is strategically equivalent to the sequential version in Figure 1(a), and
is used to illustrate the sensitivity of the logit agent quantal response
equilibrium correspondence to a game's extensive-form representation."

p "" 1 1 "" { "N" "E" } 0
p "" 2 1 "" { "F" "A" } 0
t "" 1 "" { 2, 2 }
t "" 2 "" { 2, 2 }
p "" 2 1 "" { "F" "A" } 0
t "" 3 "" { 0, 0 }
t "" 4 "" { 3, 1 }
